lane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038247/assets/c35c98904d2a0d0d6d49c582cd9f9dba9d96e91ae0da5deb2d329f38f77532e3.png)\n\nTo determine the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region, we pick four test points, one for each region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038247/assets/9340582eaad37c4ce1e0c8cbcdce48faec1e36c3c05adbedd61aa2de7168fd2f.png)\n\nNext, we calculate the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region using a sign table:\n\n|  | Test point | $-3x$ | $y$ | $f(x,y)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Top-Left | $(-1,1)$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| Top-Right | $(1,1)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| Bottom-Left | $(-1,-1)$ | $+$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n| Bottom-Right | $(1,-1)$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n\n \n\nFinally, on our diagram, we shade in the solutions to $f(x,y)\\ge 0$ using the *last* column of the table above.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038247/assets/3cfdf7d548c430f225a78fa6c4d915d69207f0a1c090d13cdd530c90865731ef.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-121252/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "490982ac-6197-58eb-8d94-2ef28d659d50"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-121252"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-149610/selection/723fe72955dc08163472a6cb719aeca3e590eb162bda88ce0b0ad0152abc2fe3" :answer/id #uuid "159ab836-558a-5d03-920c-ae8cca48d629" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038247/assets/9ca3a2fd93541dd1865f95beb53cddeb3ff1e7759e1534ae547c4b943931d24e.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149610/selection/fee66ab7e1909bff2bf51c8e142adab15b88bc58e721b9656f443e155725d23d" :answer/id #uuid "75d9eb36-08ae-52b4-82ad-ebd85e466028" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/quest